1
00:00:38,643 --> 00:00:40,270
ORIGINAL WORK TATSUKI FUJIMOTO

2
00:01:08,381 --> 00:01:10,217
It's that same dream again.

3
00:01:10,926 --> 00:01:14,262
It's that same dream I always dream...
And always forget.

4
00:01:22,229 --> 00:01:23,230
Denji.

5
00:01:25,732 --> 00:01:26,900
Pochita!

6
00:01:27,609 --> 00:01:29,361
Pochita, come out!

7
00:01:29,861 --> 00:01:32,239
We're just in a dream right now.
Let me pet you.

8
00:01:32,322 --> 00:01:33,490
Denji.

9
00:01:39,579 --> 00:01:41,248
Do not open the door. No matter what.

10
00:02:02,435 --> 00:02:04,771
What's going on? You're so loud.

11
00:02:06,982 --> 00:02:08,525
I had a bad dream.

12
00:02:18,159 --> 00:02:19,286
Am I still in a dream?

13
00:02:19,828 --> 00:02:21,288
What are you talking about?

14
00:02:27,794 --> 00:02:30,088
What's going on?

15
00:02:30,171 --> 00:02:33,341
Where did I get all this power?

16
00:02:33,425 --> 00:02:37,053
So this isn't a dream.

17
00:02:58,575 --> 00:02:59,576
CHAINSAW MAN

18
00:03:06,166 --> 00:03:07,876
PUBLIC SAFETY DEVIL HUNTERS
LARGE-SCALE ATTACK

19
00:04:34,963 --> 00:04:35,964
ONE MOMENT PLEASE.

20
00:05:06,745 --> 00:05:09,748
REZE ARC

21
00:05:12,584 --> 00:05:15,003
DEVIL HUNTER TOKYO HQ BUILDING

22
00:05:19,382 --> 00:05:21,009
What are these horns?

23
00:05:21,092 --> 00:05:24,262
Power, you drank too much blood,
didn't you?

24
00:05:24,929 --> 00:05:26,347
Maybe you drank too much blood

25
00:05:26,431 --> 00:05:28,683
in that fight against the zombies.

26
00:05:28,767 --> 00:05:31,644
-We've got to drain some blood out of you.
-Okay!

27
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:33,438
Drain her blood?

28
00:05:33,521 --> 00:05:36,024
Power has to have her blood drained
every once in a while,

29
00:05:36,816 --> 00:05:38,943
or else she becomes even more scary

30
00:05:39,027 --> 00:05:41,154
and self-centered than she normally is.

31
00:05:41,863 --> 00:05:43,782
- So that's why... Denji...
- Huh?

32
00:05:43,865 --> 00:05:46,159
Is it okay if I borrow Power for a while?

33
00:05:47,952 --> 00:05:49,037
Hmm...

34
00:05:52,624 --> 00:05:54,167
Take as long as you need.

35
00:05:56,252 --> 00:05:58,922
As for who's going to be your new buddy
while I'm borrowing her,

36
00:05:59,589 --> 00:06:01,841
this guy said
he wants to team up with you.

37
00:06:07,097 --> 00:06:09,474
Lord Chainsaw! Lord Chainsaw!

38
00:06:14,145 --> 00:06:16,272
Who is this guy?

39
00:06:16,981 --> 00:06:18,066
He's the Shark Fiend.

40
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:21,528
Normally, he's so ferocious that no one
can even have a conversation with him.

41
00:06:21,611 --> 00:06:23,863
But he said that as long as he gets
to pair up with you, Denji,

42
00:06:23,947 --> 00:06:26,866
-he'll do whatever you tell him to.
-He'll do whatever I tell him to do?

43
00:06:27,450 --> 00:06:29,911
-How come?
-I'm not sure.

44
00:06:29,994 --> 00:06:31,412
Maybe it's because your faces look alike.

45
00:06:31,496 --> 00:06:34,415
Lord Chainsaw! I'll do whatever you say!
No matter what! Lord Chainsaw!

46
00:06:34,499 --> 00:06:37,418
You're the best! You're the greatest!
Lord Chainsaw! You're the greatest!

47
00:06:37,502 --> 00:06:40,046
Don't touch me! I'm not into men.

48
00:06:45,468 --> 00:06:48,513
Hmm? You look unhappy.

49
00:06:50,765 --> 00:06:52,684
I feel great.

50
00:06:56,813 --> 00:06:58,523
If you really are feeling great,

51
00:06:58,606 --> 00:07:01,442
then how about going on a date
with me tomorrow on our day off?

52
00:07:02,402 --> 00:07:03,444
A date?

53
00:07:07,448 --> 00:07:10,952
Hooray! Hooray!

54
00:07:12,453 --> 00:07:14,706
Huh? Denji, you're already here.

55
00:07:15,290 --> 00:07:17,667
You're an hour early.

56
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:23,006
She's so cute! She's so cute!

57
00:07:23,089 --> 00:07:24,841
She's so cute!

58
00:07:25,425 --> 00:07:27,510
Denji, what time did you get here?

59
00:07:27,594 --> 00:07:30,054
I couldn't sleep last night.
I got here at 5:00.

60
00:07:30,638 --> 00:07:33,057
So... what's the plan for today?

61
00:07:33,975 --> 00:07:37,228
I've never hung out with a girl before.

62
00:07:38,062 --> 00:07:43,484
Today, from now until midnight,
we're going to go movie-theater hopping.

63
00:07:44,736 --> 00:07:45,737
What?

64
00:07:54,996 --> 00:07:58,625
Well, this isn't what I was expecting.

65
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:03,880
Everyone's laughing.

66
00:08:03,963 --> 00:08:06,382
It wasn't that funny!

67
00:08:11,471 --> 00:08:13,765
Makima's not laughing either.

68
00:08:14,515 --> 00:08:16,142
She's so cute.

69
00:08:18,311 --> 00:08:19,938
That was disappointing.

70
00:08:20,438 --> 00:08:22,273
It wasn't very interesting at all.

71
00:08:22,357 --> 00:08:25,151
It looked like they spent a lot of money
making that movie though.

72
00:08:26,653 --> 00:08:29,030
Well, then... let's go to the next one.

73
00:08:39,874 --> 00:08:41,125
Everyone's crying.

74
00:08:43,878 --> 00:08:45,713
She's not crying.

75
00:08:45,797 --> 00:08:46,798
She's so cute.

76
00:08:48,132 --> 00:08:50,134
That was disappointing.

77
00:08:50,218 --> 00:08:53,930
I didn't like how it felt
when they were trying to force us to cry.

78
00:08:58,017 --> 00:09:00,186
At least the music was good.

79
00:09:02,522 --> 00:09:04,816
The story seemed so fake.

80
00:09:09,737 --> 00:09:11,823
It was just average.

81
00:09:12,448 --> 00:09:14,200
The next movie is the last one.

82
00:09:14,284 --> 00:09:15,285
CINEMA

83
00:09:15,368 --> 00:09:18,663
Everyone says this movie
is hard to understand.

84
00:09:19,789 --> 00:09:21,416
Do you want to try watching it, Denji?

85
00:09:23,918 --> 00:09:27,213
Honestly, all the movies
we've seen today are bad.

86
00:09:27,297 --> 00:09:30,091
Maybe I don't get movies or something.

87
00:09:30,883 --> 00:09:35,513
I only find one good movie
for every ten movies I watch too.

88
00:09:35,596 --> 00:09:36,806
Huh?

89
00:09:36,889 --> 00:09:41,227
But one of those
was a movie that changed my life.

90
00:10:27,315 --> 00:10:29,317
Huh? Whoa.

91
00:10:30,443 --> 00:10:33,029
This scene isn't even that important.

92
00:10:33,654 --> 00:10:36,074
I hope Makima doesn't see me!

93
00:10:54,258 --> 00:10:58,054
I'm never going to forget that last scene
until the day I die.

94
00:10:58,137 --> 00:10:59,305
Me too.

95
00:10:59,389 --> 00:11:02,141
That last movie made
the price of the ticket worth it.

96
00:11:06,145 --> 00:11:09,899
Makima, do you think I have a heart?

97
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:13,152
Why are you asking that question?

98
00:11:14,570 --> 00:11:15,613
Just because.

99
00:11:39,303 --> 00:11:40,555
You do.

100
00:11:40,638 --> 00:11:42,723
I...

101
00:11:43,724 --> 00:11:45,143
I do.

102
00:12:13,337 --> 00:12:14,672
I see...

103
00:12:14,755 --> 00:12:18,926
The fact that I felt butterflies
means that I do have a heart!

104
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:22,013
Donations, please!
Donations, please! Donations, please!

105
00:12:22,096 --> 00:12:25,975
We're collecting donations for children
who've been victimized by devils.

106
00:12:26,601 --> 00:12:28,102
Donations, please!

107
00:12:28,186 --> 00:12:31,022
I have a heart,
so I can even make a donation!

108
00:12:32,523 --> 00:12:33,774
Thank you very much!

109
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:37,528
We're giving away flowers
to everyone who makes a donation.

110
00:12:38,154 --> 00:12:39,739
Ah...

111
00:12:40,490 --> 00:12:41,491
It's beautiful.

112
00:12:42,241 --> 00:12:43,534
Huh?

113
00:12:48,372 --> 00:12:50,374
And the fact that
I can feel that the flower is beautiful

114
00:12:50,458 --> 00:12:52,710
also means I have a heart!

115
00:12:52,793 --> 00:12:53,794
Huh?

116
00:12:55,796 --> 00:12:57,798
Makima, you're incredible.

117
00:12:58,925 --> 00:13:01,636
I feel so much better
after talking to you!

118
00:13:03,554 --> 00:13:07,558
Makima said that once I've gathered
all the pieces of the Gun Devil's flesh,

119
00:13:07,642 --> 00:13:09,101
she'll grant me one wish.

120
00:13:09,185 --> 00:13:13,064
In that case... I think I want
to ask her to be my girlfriend.

121
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:25,535
Whenever I have a free moment,
I always start thinking about Makima.

122
00:13:25,618 --> 00:13:29,372
I've squeezed other girls' boobs
and kissed other girls before too,

123
00:13:29,455 --> 00:13:32,166
but my heart belongs completely to Makima!

124
00:13:32,792 --> 00:13:35,836
There's no way I'm going
to fall for anyone else!

125
00:13:40,424 --> 00:13:42,093
Run away!

126
00:13:43,261 --> 00:13:44,345
Whoo-hoo!

127
00:13:44,428 --> 00:13:45,638
Water! Water!

128
00:13:45,721 --> 00:13:48,474
Water!

129
00:13:49,976 --> 00:13:50,977
Ah.

130
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:53,563
Beam! You stay hidden!

131
00:13:53,646 --> 00:13:56,649
If anyone sees you, I won't be able
to walk around in public anymore.

132
00:13:56,732 --> 00:13:57,733
Okay!

133
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:03,155
Why do fiends all have such weird names?

134
00:14:15,543 --> 00:14:18,129
I should have brought an umbrella.

135
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:29,640
Whoa!

136
00:14:32,226 --> 00:14:33,686
Hello, hello.

137
00:14:34,270 --> 00:14:36,397
It's raining so hard.

138
00:14:37,148 --> 00:14:39,400
Huh? Uh...

139
00:14:39,984 --> 00:14:41,944
The weather report said...

140
00:14:43,654 --> 00:14:44,697
Hmm?

141
00:14:45,489 --> 00:14:48,034
Huh?

142
00:14:49,201 --> 00:14:50,620
Huh? What's wrong?

143
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:52,955
Sorry.

144
00:14:54,373 --> 00:14:55,875
What's wrong with you?

145
00:15:00,671 --> 00:15:03,341
Huh? How come you're crying?

146
00:15:03,424 --> 00:15:05,051
Sorry.

147
00:15:05,801 --> 00:15:07,011
Your face...

148
00:15:07,595 --> 00:15:09,889
looks like my dog that passed away.

149
00:15:09,972 --> 00:15:13,309
Huh? You're saying I'm a dog?

150
00:15:13,392 --> 00:15:15,936
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

151
00:15:20,274 --> 00:15:22,318
Hmm? Are you okay?

152
00:15:25,321 --> 00:15:26,781
Uh...

153
00:15:28,991 --> 00:15:31,452
Hold on! I've got a handkerchief!

154
00:15:34,038 --> 00:15:35,790
Ta-da!

155
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:37,917
What?

156
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,043
A magic trick?

157
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:41,003
That's amazing!

158
00:15:41,837 --> 00:15:44,340
There's no trick to it.

159
00:15:48,135 --> 00:15:49,345
Thanks.

160
00:16:03,609 --> 00:16:05,444
Ah. It stopped raining!

161
00:16:06,862 --> 00:16:10,199
I work at a café called Crossroads
right down there.

162
00:16:10,282 --> 00:16:12,451
If you drop by,
I'll pay you back for this.

163
00:16:13,577 --> 00:16:15,037
Make sure you come, okay?

164
00:16:56,996 --> 00:16:57,997
All right.

165
00:16:58,622 --> 00:17:01,625
You're late.
I'm going to deduct it from your pay.

166
00:17:01,709 --> 00:17:02,752
You're so stingy!

167
00:17:03,377 --> 00:17:05,129
Take this water to table four.

168
00:17:05,212 --> 00:17:07,882
Stingy! Stingy! Stingy! Stingy! Stingy!

169
00:17:11,969 --> 00:17:14,263
Th... That was fast!

170
00:17:14,346 --> 00:17:17,808
Huh? You got here faster than me!

171
00:17:17,892 --> 00:17:19,894
Well, I guess you're right.

172
00:17:21,395 --> 00:17:23,522
I just came so that you could pay me back.

173
00:17:23,606 --> 00:17:25,483
Hmm?

174
00:17:29,153 --> 00:17:31,781
-Oh.
-Let's have a drink together!

175
00:17:31,864 --> 00:17:35,409
Hey! Can you bring some coffee
for me and him?

176
00:17:36,202 --> 00:17:38,037
But you work here.

177
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,039
What's the big deal?

178
00:17:40,122 --> 00:17:42,792
We only get customers
in the morning anyway.

179
00:17:45,085 --> 00:17:46,337
Well...

180
00:17:47,797 --> 00:17:49,799
A cup of coffee is my gift back to you!

181
00:17:50,716 --> 00:17:51,801
Do you like coffee?

182
00:17:52,468 --> 00:17:53,594
I'll drink it.

183
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:02,144
What's with that face?
You're just pretending you're fine!

184
00:18:02,228 --> 00:18:04,313
Coffee tastes bad!

185
00:18:04,396 --> 00:18:06,315
It tastes like it's from the gutter!

186
00:18:09,485 --> 00:18:11,237
You're just like a little kid!

187
00:18:13,364 --> 00:18:16,951
She's touching me a lot,
and she's laughing at my jokes.

188
00:18:17,451 --> 00:18:18,744
Could it be that...

189
00:18:19,537 --> 00:18:21,121
she likes me?

190
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,333
My name's Reze.

191
00:18:24,834 --> 00:18:25,876
What's your name?

192
00:18:26,877 --> 00:18:27,962
Denji.

193
00:18:28,879 --> 00:18:29,880
Denji?

194
00:18:30,714 --> 00:18:32,091
Denji...

195
00:18:36,262 --> 00:18:39,557
Denji, I've never met someone
as interesting as you.

196
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:43,352
Huh...

197
00:18:43,435 --> 00:18:45,729
I'm sure about it now. She does like me.

198
00:18:47,189 --> 00:18:48,649
What am I going to do?

199
00:18:49,275 --> 00:18:51,861
I like people who like me too.

200
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:55,155
Makima... help.

201
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:59,243
I'm going to start falling for this girl.

202
00:19:15,384 --> 00:19:17,928
You've had three already. That's enough.

203
00:19:18,012 --> 00:19:19,430
We're going to go on patrol now.

204
00:19:21,307 --> 00:19:23,767
Eating ice cream made me tired.

205
00:19:23,851 --> 00:19:26,312
I heard that eating takes energy too.

206
00:19:31,734 --> 00:19:34,194
I don't want to work anymore today.

207
00:19:35,070 --> 00:19:36,739
They found out where the Gun Devil is.

208
00:19:36,822 --> 00:19:38,198
There's going to be an expedition.

209
00:19:38,282 --> 00:19:43,078
In order to participate, I need to have
more experience defeating big devils.

210
00:19:43,787 --> 00:19:47,207
That's why I want to
go look for more devils.

211
00:19:47,291 --> 00:19:50,628
You're my buddy. Please help me out.

212
00:19:50,711 --> 00:19:52,004
Huh?

213
00:19:55,174 --> 00:19:56,800
Hmm...

214
00:20:00,304 --> 00:20:03,057
How about I think about it a bit
after I've had another ice cream?

215
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,601
Get up.

216
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:08,687
If I tell the leadership
that you're useless,

217
00:20:08,771 --> 00:20:11,899
they're going to kill you as a devil.
Are you sure you're okay with that?

218
00:20:13,442 --> 00:20:14,944
Hmm.

219
00:20:19,657 --> 00:20:22,576
I'd rather die than work.

220
00:20:25,913 --> 00:20:28,540
He's the second-most
powerful member of Division 4,

221
00:20:28,624 --> 00:20:29,708
after Captain Kishibe.

222
00:20:31,085 --> 00:20:33,754
At least he would be
if he weren't always so lazy.

223
00:20:34,588 --> 00:20:37,800
If you want to join the expedition
to defeat the Gun Devil,

224
00:20:37,883 --> 00:20:40,636
then you should try
to make good use of him.

225
00:20:41,971 --> 00:20:44,515
I don't think
I can get along well with a devil.

226
00:20:45,140 --> 00:20:48,018
But you get along with Power, right?

227
00:20:48,519 --> 00:20:51,563
We had a fistfight just this morning.

228
00:20:53,524 --> 00:20:56,276
You don't have to become friends.

229
00:20:57,027 --> 00:20:59,947
Just use him for your own benefit.

230
00:21:00,531 --> 00:21:02,825
He's someone
who killed every single person

231
00:21:02,908 --> 00:21:05,160
in the village where he was born.

232
00:21:05,244 --> 00:21:06,704
Or to put it more accurately:

233
00:21:07,413 --> 00:21:10,457
He sucked the lifespans out of them
and transformed them into weapons.

234
00:21:11,208 --> 00:21:12,209
Weapons?

235
00:21:12,793 --> 00:21:16,547
He has the power to transform the
life of anyone he touches into a weapon.

236
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:20,467
That katana you have
is one of his weapons too.

237
00:21:20,551 --> 00:21:24,054
Those weapons can do things like cut
through ghosts that no one can touch...

238
00:21:24,138 --> 00:21:26,473
and have different special powers.

239
00:21:28,308 --> 00:21:31,395
It's okay if you have to pretend.
Just be friendly with him.

240
00:21:31,478 --> 00:21:33,981
I'm sure he'll be useful to you.

241
00:21:55,294 --> 00:21:56,879
I've eliminated the devil!

242
00:21:57,379 --> 00:22:00,924
Please make sure
not to touch its blood or its flesh!

243
00:22:07,681 --> 00:22:09,892
Whoa, that looks delicious.

244
00:22:12,019 --> 00:22:13,645
Hey you, human.

245
00:22:13,729 --> 00:22:15,230
Come over here.

246
00:22:16,398 --> 00:22:19,359
He must be a private Devil Hunter.

247
00:22:19,443 --> 00:22:21,904
He was being eaten up by this devil.

248
00:22:21,987 --> 00:22:25,157
The lower half of his body
is gone already. He's almost dead.

249
00:22:30,829 --> 00:22:33,916
Kill me. Kill me.

250
00:22:34,541 --> 00:22:37,294
Your power gives you
the ability to kill him painlessly.

251
00:22:37,377 --> 00:22:38,796
Grant him his wish to die.

252
00:22:39,296 --> 00:22:40,672
Huh? No way.

253
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:43,675
I may be an angel, but I'm also a devil.

254
00:22:44,384 --> 00:22:47,137
I believe that humans
should suffer when they die.

255
00:23:06,281 --> 00:23:08,826
I don't think we can become friends.
Even if I pretend.

256
00:23:10,077 --> 00:23:11,078
I guess not.

257
00:23:14,706 --> 00:23:17,960
Makima's the one
who found my heart.

258
00:23:18,544 --> 00:23:22,339
So that's why my heart belongs to Makima.

259
00:23:23,841 --> 00:23:26,343
But... my body...

260
00:23:26,426 --> 00:23:27,928
It's moving on its own!

261
00:23:30,097 --> 00:23:32,224
Oh, it's you!

262
00:23:32,307 --> 00:23:33,851
I came to have lunch.

263
00:23:34,935 --> 00:23:38,939
The food here's not that good. No one
would come every day for a whole week.

