Huh?

527
00:49:19,311 --> 00:49:21,980
Run away! Run away!
We're in trouble! We're in trouble!

528
00:49:22,064 --> 00:49:25,109
How come I didn't notice anything
from the smell?

529
00:49:25,192 --> 00:49:27,611
She's dangerous, Lord Chainsaw!

530
00:49:27,695 --> 00:49:30,531
That smell...

531
00:49:31,198 --> 00:49:34,910
She's the Bomb Devil!

532
00:49:38,956 --> 00:49:40,332
Boom.

533
00:50:06,191 --> 00:50:07,192
You thief.

534
00:50:35,220 --> 00:50:36,513
Lord Chainsaw!

535
00:50:50,652 --> 00:50:53,322
Are you from Division 4 too?

536
00:50:53,405 --> 00:50:56,241
I'll let you go if you leave Denji there
and leave right now.

537
00:51:04,082 --> 00:51:05,793
Oh. I see.

538
00:51:20,265 --> 00:51:21,767
Hmm?

539
00:51:35,531 --> 00:51:38,992
Damn. I wanted to go to the festival.

540
00:51:39,493 --> 00:51:41,662
Whoa. She's killing something.

541
00:51:41,745 --> 00:51:44,206
We've encountered a devil
near the festival.

542
00:51:45,165 --> 00:51:47,209
2034.

543
00:51:47,876 --> 00:51:49,628
The battle begins.

544
00:51:50,295 --> 00:51:52,714
Are you private Devil Hunters?

545
00:51:52,798 --> 00:51:54,800
Whoa. She said something.

546
00:51:54,883 --> 00:51:56,885
This one's really strong.

547
00:52:17,906 --> 00:52:19,408
They sure ran away fast!

548
00:52:20,576 --> 00:52:22,494
DEVIL EXTERMINATION DIVISION 2
FUCHŪ TRAINING FACILITY

549
00:52:34,548 --> 00:52:35,674
Match over!

550
00:52:36,300 --> 00:52:38,010
Thank you.

551
00:52:40,304 --> 00:52:43,015
Thank you for your instruction.

552
00:52:44,391 --> 00:52:45,726
Aki.

553
00:52:46,602 --> 00:52:49,354
Thanks for coming.

554
00:52:49,438 --> 00:52:51,440
I can't say no to you, Nomo.

555
00:52:51,523 --> 00:52:55,736
Whoa! Really?
Then come back to Division 2!

556
00:52:55,819 --> 00:52:59,364
All the stories I hear about
the Special Division sound so gory anyway.

557
00:52:59,448 --> 00:53:03,535
If everything goes well, I'm going
to become the sub-captain in five years.

558
00:53:03,619 --> 00:53:06,121
When that happens,
I'm going to invite you to join.

559
00:53:07,915 --> 00:53:09,374
Thank you very much.

560
00:53:12,586 --> 00:53:13,629
Hey.

561
00:53:14,254 --> 00:53:16,715
You haven't told him
that you'll be dead in five years?

562
00:53:17,883 --> 00:53:20,385
Who did you hear that from?

563
00:53:20,469 --> 00:53:21,887
From Power.

564
00:53:22,512 --> 00:53:23,972
That damn devil.

565
00:53:25,474 --> 00:53:27,017
Don't tell anyone.

566
00:53:28,727 --> 00:53:30,520
You're so lucky.

567
00:53:30,604 --> 00:53:32,689
I want to die soon too.

568
00:53:33,857 --> 00:53:36,568
As long as I'm alive, I have to work hard.

569
00:53:36,652 --> 00:53:38,737
If I die,
I won't have to work hard anymore.

570
00:53:40,238 --> 00:53:41,740
Oh, that reminds me...

571
00:53:42,324 --> 00:53:44,701
You have a contract
with the Future Devil, right?

572
00:53:45,202 --> 00:53:46,912
Why don't you try asking it?

573
00:53:46,995 --> 00:53:48,705
Ask it when I'm going to die.

574
00:53:49,957 --> 00:53:51,166
I refuse.

575
00:53:52,751 --> 00:53:55,545
Aki! Come downstairs! Now!

576
00:53:57,381 --> 00:54:00,258
He showed up at the entrance and
claimed he's from the Special Division.

577
00:54:01,259 --> 00:54:03,929
Is this fiend really on our side?

578
00:54:04,012 --> 00:54:05,430
Y-Yes.

579
00:54:05,931 --> 00:54:09,184
Did a devil do this to Denji?

580
00:54:10,268 --> 00:54:13,063
Bomb is coming... Bomb...

581
00:54:13,730 --> 00:54:16,316
She's one of the Gun Devil's allies!

582
00:54:18,402 --> 00:54:20,696
How do you know that?

583
00:54:23,115 --> 00:54:24,199
Answer me.

584
00:54:24,825 --> 00:54:27,452
I could kill you right here
if I wanted to.

585
00:54:28,537 --> 00:54:30,580
If I tell you, they'll kill me.

586
00:54:30,664 --> 00:54:32,457
I promised Makima.

587
00:54:32,541 --> 00:54:33,959
Makima?

588
00:54:34,042 --> 00:54:35,585
Ah!

589
00:54:35,669 --> 00:54:37,713
There she is! Bomb's here!

590
00:54:45,512 --> 00:54:46,888
Hey, beautiful lady!

591
00:54:47,514 --> 00:54:49,516
Don't come any closer!

592
00:54:50,017 --> 00:54:52,728
This place is a training facility
for Devil Extermination Division 2.

593
00:54:52,811 --> 00:54:55,564
Members of the public
are not allowed to enter.

594
00:54:57,357 --> 00:54:59,192
Excuse me!

595
00:55:01,278 --> 00:55:02,320
Reze...

596
00:55:02,404 --> 00:55:03,697
Reze?

597
00:55:03,780 --> 00:55:06,241
Please help me!

598
00:55:06,324 --> 00:55:08,952
I'm being attacked by a devil!

599
00:55:09,578 --> 00:55:10,579
Oh.

600
00:55:10,662 --> 00:55:13,290
She's sure smiling a lot
for someone under attack.

601
00:55:13,373 --> 00:55:15,250
-Nomo.
-Yeah.

602
00:55:15,333 --> 00:55:17,461
Take your friend with you
and stay in the back.

603
00:55:17,544 --> 00:55:18,712
Okay.

604
00:55:18,795 --> 00:55:22,632
Contact headquarters and the vice-captain.
Summon all Division 2 members.

605
00:55:22,716 --> 00:55:24,176
Okay!

606
00:55:24,259 --> 00:55:25,343
And...

607
00:55:26,011 --> 00:55:28,722
Have you seen that beauty
somewhere before?

608
00:55:29,306 --> 00:55:31,725
Now's not the right time
to try to pick up women.

609
00:55:31,808 --> 00:55:34,227
No, I'm being serious.

610
00:55:37,522 --> 00:55:40,609
It can't be true. There's no way.

611
00:55:40,692 --> 00:55:43,361
Thanks. I'm counting on you.

612
00:55:43,445 --> 00:55:44,738
You owe me one.

613
00:55:46,656 --> 00:55:48,241
Kato! Tanabe!

614
00:55:49,117 --> 00:55:51,703
I'll treat you to dinner
if you can kill that woman.

615
00:55:51,787 --> 00:55:54,748
Don't assume she's a human.
Handle her like you would a devil.

616
00:55:55,373 --> 00:55:58,085
I guess it didn't work.

617
00:55:58,168 --> 00:55:59,628
It's not working.

618
00:56:00,921 --> 00:56:02,631
In that case, I've got no choice.

619
00:56:04,758 --> 00:56:07,010
I'll just have to kill everyone.

620
00:56:13,350 --> 00:56:14,518
Blood?

621
00:56:14,601 --> 00:56:17,187
We've caused mold to grow
in her heart and intestines.

622
00:56:17,687 --> 00:56:20,273
She's throwing up blood. It's working.

623
00:56:20,357 --> 00:56:23,276
Even if she drinks blood and regenerates,
the mold's not going to disappear.

624
00:56:24,194 --> 00:56:26,279
Now we just need to buy some time.

625
00:56:29,366 --> 00:56:30,534
Hmm?

626
00:56:33,620 --> 00:56:35,080
She inflicted damage to herself!

627
00:56:37,916 --> 00:56:39,626
Are you able to grow mold on her brain?

628
00:56:39,709 --> 00:56:41,837
We can only do it if the target's alive.

629
00:56:51,513 --> 00:56:52,556
Boo.

630
00:57:00,438 --> 00:57:02,858
She's a devil! A devil is here!

631
00:57:02,941 --> 00:57:05,694
She went right!
Don't let her get near Aki!

632
00:57:05,777 --> 00:57:07,404
Nomo! Behind you!

633
00:57:09,906 --> 00:57:11,158
Kon!

634
00:57:15,620 --> 00:57:17,080
Ah--

635
00:57:28,758 --> 00:57:31,511
There she is! There's the devil!

636
00:57:34,973 --> 00:57:37,517
Masaki Ando,
requesting permission to fire!

637
00:57:37,601 --> 00:57:38,894
Permission granted!

638
00:57:50,363 --> 00:57:52,616
In Japan,
do you need permission to fire a gun?

639
00:57:53,950 --> 00:57:54,951
Kon!

640
00:58:00,957 --> 00:58:02,959
You're pretty stubborn.

641
00:58:04,044 --> 00:58:06,880
Now that's a real sight for sore eyes.

642
00:58:12,469 --> 00:58:13,678
Kon.

643
00:58:20,602 --> 00:58:22,520
Excuse me for a moment.

644
00:58:22,604 --> 00:58:24,272
Vice-captain!

645
00:58:24,356 --> 00:58:27,359
That was close.

646
00:58:28,568 --> 00:58:31,154
What's that taste?

647
00:58:31,238 --> 00:58:34,491
- Huh?
- I hate this taste.

648
00:58:34,574 --> 00:58:35,700
I'm going home now.

649
00:58:40,372 --> 00:58:42,832
I was supposed to go
to a singles mixer today.

650
00:58:43,333 --> 00:58:46,086
Take me with you next time.

651
00:58:48,004 --> 00:58:51,383
I'll drive. You have them
drink some of your blood.

652
00:58:51,466 --> 00:58:52,968
Huh?

653
00:58:53,051 --> 00:58:54,636
I guess I've got no choice.

654
00:58:58,223 --> 00:59:00,642
Aren't you going to start the car?

655
00:59:01,476 --> 00:59:02,894
Damn.

656
00:59:03,478 --> 00:59:06,398
It showed me a future
I didn't want to see.

657
00:59:06,481 --> 00:59:07,482
Huh?

658
00:59:18,743 --> 00:59:20,412
That monster.

659
00:59:20,495 --> 00:59:24,165
I killed them to show you
how powerful I am.

660
00:59:24,249 --> 00:59:26,543
I don't want to kill anyone if possible.

661
00:59:27,877 --> 00:59:30,880
Take Denji out of the car and leave.

662
00:59:45,979 --> 00:59:49,691
The gasoline is going to
make that car burn to a crisp.

663
00:59:53,862 --> 00:59:56,239
What a pain.

664
00:59:57,782 --> 00:59:59,284
Acho!

665
01:00:03,872 --> 01:00:05,874
I asked the Special Division for backup.

666
01:00:05,957 --> 01:00:07,167
They saved us.

667
01:00:13,757 --> 01:00:15,133
No way!

668
01:00:16,676 --> 01:00:19,637
I kicked with everything I got just now.

669
01:00:20,597 --> 01:00:22,182
Nice kick.

670
01:00:25,769 --> 01:00:27,020
Want to fight?

671
01:00:28,563 --> 01:00:31,649
Kobeni! We're changing strategies!

672
01:00:32,984 --> 01:00:36,112
This one's a lot stronger than us!

673
01:00:36,196 --> 01:00:38,406
Time for a strategic retreat!

674
01:00:38,990 --> 01:00:40,450
Anyways, bye.

675
01:00:45,705 --> 01:00:48,291
My legs... My legs...

676
01:00:48,375 --> 01:00:50,126
My legs gave out...

677
01:00:51,336 --> 01:00:54,130
My legs... My legs...

678
01:00:59,219 --> 01:01:02,138
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

679
01:01:02,222 --> 01:01:04,974
I'll quit my job. So please forgive me!

680
01:01:25,537 --> 01:01:26,538
There she is!

681
01:01:34,254 --> 01:01:37,924
Hey. Chainsaw's awake now.

682
01:01:38,007 --> 01:01:40,468
But the bomb girl's right behind us.

683
01:01:42,011 --> 01:01:44,055
Shit! Damn!

684
01:01:44,139 --> 01:01:47,058
The transmitter's broken on this car.

685
01:01:48,476 --> 01:01:50,145
What's wrong with this car?

686
01:01:51,271 --> 01:01:54,065
If it comes down to it,
I'm going to crash this car into her!

687
01:01:54,149 --> 01:01:56,818
I can't let her have Denji!

688
01:01:58,653 --> 01:02:00,405
What's going on?

689
01:02:00,488 --> 01:02:02,449
He's cutting the top of the car!

690
01:02:02,532 --> 01:02:03,658
Huh?

691
01:02:06,619 --> 01:02:07,912
Stop, Denji!

692
01:02:07,996 --> 01:02:09,914
You haven't had that much blood yet!

693
01:02:11,124 --> 01:02:14,252
It hurt so much,
I thought I was going to die.

694
01:02:14,335 --> 01:02:17,338
My brain's all mixed-up.

695
01:02:17,422 --> 01:02:19,966
But I spent some time
looking back on what's happened.

696
01:02:21,301 --> 01:02:24,220
And I just realized

697
01:02:24,304 --> 01:02:27,807
that every single girl I ever meet
always tries to kill me!

698
01:02:28,391 --> 01:02:32,145
Everyone always wants Chainsaw's heart!

699
01:02:32,228 --> 01:02:36,316
Doesn't anyone want Denji's heart? Huh?

700
01:02:36,399 --> 01:02:40,069
I really do like you, Denji. It's true.

701
01:02:40,153 --> 01:02:42,071
Huh? Really?

702
01:02:44,657 --> 01:02:47,994
Don't listen to the enemy!
You're so gullible!

703
01:02:50,371 --> 01:02:53,833
That was close.
I was about to get tricked.

704
01:02:54,417 --> 01:02:57,629
I don't know why you're trying to kill me.

705
01:02:57,712 --> 01:02:59,839
But I don't care!

706
01:03:00,548 --> 01:03:02,592
I've got Makima!

707
01:03:03,426 --> 01:03:04,844
Makima?

708
01:03:04,928 --> 01:03:09,474
Denji, I didn't know that witch
has got you in the palm of her hand.

709
01:03:09,557 --> 01:03:12,602
Then it would have been no use
even if we ran away together.

710
01:03:12,685 --> 01:03:14,270
Aw.

711
01:03:14,354 --> 01:03:17,607
I wish I never kissed you! Aw.

712
01:03:20,818 --> 01:03:22,153
If anyone else dies because of me,

713
01:03:22,237 --> 01:03:25,073
I'm going to have trouble getting
out of bed in the morning.

714
01:03:26,199 --> 01:03:28,868
I'm going to arrest you!

715
01:03:28,952 --> 01:03:30,870
Come here, Denji.

716
01:03:30,954 --> 01:03:34,624
I'm going to show you how we fight.

717
01:03:34,707 --> 01:03:37,335
Then show me!

718
01:04:00,191 --> 01:04:03,319
Denji. You're not applying
what you've learned.

719
01:04:03,403 --> 01:04:06,155
You can't just swing
your chainsaws around.

720
01:04:06,239 --> 01:04:08,950
You've got to understand
your own power better.

721
01:04:09,033 --> 01:04:10,076
Huh?

722
01:04:13,705 --> 01:04:14,747
Boom.

723
01:05:08,718 --> 01:05:10,011
Regeneration?

724
01:05:11,054 --> 01:05:12,639
So you were revving the engine

725
01:05:12,722 --> 01:05:14,932
before you got kicked.

726
01:05:49,258 --> 01:05:50,593
You Devil!

727
01:06:10,738 --> 01:06:12,990
If I mess up even
a single move, I'm going to die.

728
01:06:13,658 --> 01:06:17,120
I can see the future,
but only a few seconds in advance.

729
01:06:17,704 --> 01:06:20,081
I don't know if my body
will be able to react in time.

730
01:06:26,045 --> 01:06:27,672
Perfect judgment.

731
01:06:32,969 --> 01:06:34,178
Perfect judgment.

732
01:06:36,222 --> 01:06:38,015
Perfect judgment.

733
01:06:43,813 --> 01:06:45,231
Perfect--

734
01:06:52,697 --> 01:06:53,906
That was close!

735
01:06:53,990 --> 01:06:56,909
Sorry I'm late.

736
01:06:57,493 --> 01:07:00,079
This is the first time I've ever
wanted to be friends with a Devil!

737
01:07:00,163 --> 01:07:01,414
Here you go.

738
01:07:04,917 --> 01:07:07,086
Time-out!

739
01:07:07,170 --> 01:07:09,922
I'm anemic
and I'm almost naked over here.

740
01:07:10,006 --> 01:07:12,175
And you've got the two of you.
That's not fair.

741
01:07:12,258 --> 01:07:15,678
You're right. Should we give her a break?

742
01:07:15,762 --> 01:07:17,054
No.

743
01:07:17,138 --> 01:07:19,182
That's what he said. Sorry!

744
01:07:19,265 --> 01:07:20,391
The time-out is over.

745
01:07:26,606 --> 01:07:30,818
Lady Reze! Typhoon is here!

746
01:07:31,986 --> 01:07:33,905
That's not fair!

747
01:07:52,924 --> 01:07:54,008
It's okay.

748
01:07:54,842 --> 01:07:56,761
You're going to go to heaven.

749
01:08:02,016 --> 01:08:03,810
I'm going to take your blood.

750
01:08:03,893 --> 01:08:05,061
Sorry.

751
01:08:26,249 --> 01:08:29,085
A normal devil would have been dead.

752
01:08:29,168 --> 01:08:32,213
You're so impressive, Lord Chainsaw!
You're amazing!

753
01:08:33,130 --> 01:08:36,092
Your girlfriend has killed
too many people.

754
01:08:36,175 --> 01:08:39,470
If we let her run free,
then many more will die.

755
01:08:40,429 --> 01:08:43,099
Chainsaw. Make your choice.

756
01:08:43,182 --> 01:08:47,103
Either let her kill you
and minimize the damage,

757
01:08:47,186 --> 01:08:48,938
or kill her instead.

758
01:08:51,065 --> 01:08:54,318
Well, that's an easy decision.

759
01:08:55,444 --> 01:08:57,905
Reze is incredibly powerful, though.

760
01:08:59,991 --> 01:09:03,411
Shark, you know
about the Chainsaw Devil, right?

761
01:09:03,995 --> 01:09:07,498
If you don't want to die today,
then you should tell us what you know.

762
01:09:09,500 --> 01:09:12,670
Lord Chainsaw runs really fast!

763
01:09:12,753 --> 01:09:17,508
But when he goes places,
he doesn't just use his legs.

764
01:09:17,592 --> 01:09:20,219
He uses the chains on his chainsaws
to get around.

765
01:09:20,303 --> 01:09:22,096
He flings his chains through the air
and hooks them on buildings,

766
01:09:22,179 --> 01:09:24,140
and then he swings
from building to building!

767
01:09:24,223 --> 01:09:28,436
I see! Samurai Sword
draws his sword to get around.

768
01:09:28,519 --> 01:09:31,188
And Reze uses explosions.

769
01:09:31,272 --> 01:09:33,566
I need to apply my own powers too!

770
01:09:33,649 --> 01:09:36,861
Lord Chainsaw, you're a genius!
Lord Chainsaw, you're a genius!

771
01:09:36,944 --> 01:09:41,616
I should use chains to get around!
I see! I get it!

772
01:09:43,326 --> 01:09:46,120
That's right! That's right!

773
01:09:46,203 --> 01:09:47,997
I'm going to try it!

774
01:09:48,080 --> 01:09:50,917
-Beam! Turn into a shark!
-Okay!

775
01:09:53,377 --> 01:09:54,378
Huh?

776
01:09:55,463 --> 01:09:57,924
This is it!

777
01:09:59,216 --> 01:10:04,555
I'm going to use chains to control Beam,
and Beam is going to run like a horse!

778
01:10:06,182 --> 01:10:08,809
That's not it...
That's not it...

779
01:10:08,893 --> 01:10:11,395
Are you sure? I don't think that's it.

780
01:10:11,479 --> 01:10:14,357
I think you're supposed to shoot out
the chains from your arms

781
01:10:14,440 --> 01:10:16,025
and hook them onto buildings.

782
01:10:16,108 --> 01:10:19,779
Huh? This is the right way! Right, Beam?

783
01:10:19,862 --> 01:10:22,031
You're right! You're right! You're right!

784
01:10:22,114 --> 01:10:24,450
All right! Run, Beam!

785
01:10:24,533 --> 01:10:27,453
You're right!

786
01:10:27,536 --> 01:10:29,038
You're right! You're right!

787
01:10:36,671 --> 01:10:39,423
What are you doing?

788
01:10:40,299 --> 01:10:41,550
Denji!

789
01:10:42,176 --> 01:10:44,637
There you are, Chainsaw!

790
01:10:44,720 --> 01:10:48,265
Denji! I'm going to make you
regret coming back to life!

791
01:10:49,600 --> 01:10:53,813
Beam! Don't make me regret this!

792
01:10:53,896 --> 01:10:55,106
Okay!

793
01:10:57,316 --> 01:10:59,235
Damn! Those guys...

794
01:10:59,819 --> 01:11:01,237
It's a monster battle!

795
01:11:01,320 --> 01:11:04,115
We're just going to
have to sit it out and watch.

796
01:11:17,086 --> 01:11:20,089
You keep missing!

797
01:11:20,172 --> 01:11:21,882
You're like a cockroach.

798
01:11:21,966 --> 01:11:25,094
I'm tired of the explosions!

799
01:11:25,177 --> 01:11:27,388
Chainsaw!

800
01:11:38,190 --> 01:11:40,192
-Take that!
-Ouch!

801
01:11:42,236 --> 01:11:44,530
What a waste.

802
01:11:44,613 --> 01:11:47,199
I cut off a beautiful woman's leg.

803
01:11:47,283 --> 01:11:50,494
Lady Reze! Take my blood!

804
01:11:56,000 --> 01:11:57,918
Oh! Good!

805
01:11:58,002 --> 01:11:59,378
Wait, that's not good!

806
01:11:59,879 --> 01:12:02,923
This is crazy.

807
01:12:04,633 --> 01:12:05,634
Oh!

808
01:12:13,517 --> 01:12:15,061
Grab on to something!

809
01:12:15,811 --> 01:12:18,189
I can't! I can't!

810
01:12:27,406 --> 01:12:28,407
It's okay.

811
01:12:29,992 --> 01:12:32,912
It's okay! You can let go!

812
01:12:32,995 --> 01:12:36,916
If I'm going to die, I don't care!
It just means today was my day to die.

813
01:12:37,500 --> 01:12:38,918
I'll be fine.

814
01:12:39,627 --> 01:12:42,171
I've been ready to die for a long time.

815
01:13:09,406 --> 01:13:11,450
Why?

816
01:13:11,534 --> 01:13:13,410
Why did you touch my hand?

817
01:13:13,494 --> 01:13:16,247
-Do you want to die?
-Of course I don't want to die!

818
01:13:20,793 --> 01:13:23,712
How much did my lifespan
decrease just now?

819
01:13:27,299 --> 01:13:28,425
About two months.

820
01:13:35,724 --> 01:13:38,978
If you want to die,
then die somewhere far away from me.

821
01:13:40,020 --> 01:13:42,064
I can't take it anymore,
watching someone die

822
01:13:42,773 --> 01:13:44,400
right in front of me.

823
01:14:05,462 --> 01:14:07,923
Lord Chainsaw!
We're in trouble! Something's coming!

824
01:14:08,591 --> 01:14:10,509
Lord Chainsaw--

825
01:14:15,306 --> 01:14:17,141
Hmm? Huh?

826
01:14:39,914 --> 01:14:42,791
Lord Chainsaw!

827
01:15:46,272 --> 01:15:47,773
Whoa.

828
01:15:56,031 --> 01:15:57,950
You were hanging in there
for a pretty long time.

829
01:15:59,618 --> 01:16:00,828
But I think it's time now...

830
01:16:03,455 --> 01:16:04,957
to put an end to this.

831
01:16:16,260 --> 01:16:18,220
That was close!

832
01:16:19,388 --> 01:16:20,514
Beam!

833
01:16:20,597 --> 01:16:24,018
Lord Chainsaw!
I'll make sure you won't regret this!

834
01:16:34,570 --> 01:16:36,280
Hey! This is bad!

835
01:16:36,363 --> 01:16:38,741
He's going to turn the whole city
into mincemeat at this rate!

836
01:16:38,824 --> 01:16:42,578
Beam! We've got to get
that fat-ass to shut up first!

837
01:16:42,661 --> 01:16:43,746
Okay!

838
01:16:55,049 --> 01:16:57,051
I found you!

839
01:17:02,973 --> 01:17:06,560
Die! Chainsaw!

840
01:17:35,631 --> 01:17:36,799
Yeah!

841
01:17:37,508 --> 01:17:40,010
Beam! Send me flying!

842
01:17:40,094 --> 01:17:42,012
Yeah!

843
01:17:49,603 --> 01:17:52,314
This makes it easy for me!

844
01:17:52,398 --> 01:17:55,692
All I have to do
is swing my chainsaws around...

845
01:17:56,276 --> 01:17:59,405
like crazy!

846
01:18:03,617 --> 01:18:04,785
Whoa!

847
01:18:06,036 --> 01:18:08,330
Beam!

848
01:18:08,414 --> 01:18:11,166
Lord Chainsaw!

849
01:18:29,518 --> 01:18:31,937
Stay away!

850
01:18:35,649 --> 01:18:37,568
Come on!

851
01:19:12,686 --> 01:19:14,605
We did it! Beam!

852
01:19:14,688 --> 01:19:16,231
Where's Reze?

853
01:19:17,691 --> 01:19:19,359
Ah! Lord Chainsaw!

854
01:20:17,960 --> 01:20:19,294
Whoa!

855
01:21:06,133 --> 01:21:07,509
Ouch!

856
01:21:07,593 --> 01:21:09,136
You saved me, Beam!

857
01:21:12,264 --> 01:21:15,934
Denji. Don't you think
it's about time you gave up?

858
01:21:16,560 --> 01:21:17,894
Uh...

859
01:21:18,687 --> 01:21:19,688
No.

860
01:21:40,292 --> 01:21:44,212
You're being a huge pain in the ass.
Just hurry up and die already.

861
01:21:44,838 --> 01:21:50,093
Then you should have just
killed me when we first met!

862
01:21:52,220 --> 01:21:53,722
There's nowhere left to run.

863
01:21:54,473 --> 01:21:55,724
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

864
01:21:56,350 --> 01:21:59,936
You shouldn't have taught me how to swim.

865
01:22:00,020 --> 01:22:02,689
Huh... You're going to swim?

866
01:22:32,052 --> 01:22:33,470
Chains?

867
01:22:52,823 --> 01:22:56,952
Can you still explode when you're wet?

868
01:24:44,976 --> 01:24:46,436
I can't believe it.

869
01:24:47,479 --> 01:24:49,898
Why did you resurrect me?

870
01:24:52,275 --> 01:24:55,028
I have a great life.

871
01:24:55,695 --> 01:24:59,699
No matter how many times
I get beat up or die,

872
01:24:59,783 --> 01:25:03,370
as long as I get to eat good food
the next day, I can forgive.

873
01:25:04,746 --> 01:25:05,747
But...

874
01:25:07,207 --> 01:25:10,168
if I capture you and hand you over
to Public Safety,

875
01:25:10,752 --> 01:25:14,673
I'd feel like I had a fish bone
stuck in my throat.

876
01:25:18,844 --> 01:25:21,471
Even if I were living
a good life every day,

877
01:25:21,555 --> 01:25:24,850
it would feel bad, having something
poking the back of my throat.

878
01:25:30,272 --> 01:25:33,775
Do you think you would
still say that if I killed you right now?

879
01:25:35,735 --> 01:25:37,654
If someone's going to kill me,

880
01:25:37,737 --> 01:25:39,281
then I'd rather be killed
by a beautiful woman.

881
01:25:50,375 --> 01:25:51,585
Ah...

882
01:25:53,169 --> 01:25:58,258
Do you really still believe
that I like you for real?

883
01:25:59,384 --> 01:26:03,763
The look on my face when I met you,
and the way I blushed... It was all a lie.

884
01:26:04,681 --> 01:26:06,683
I just trained myself how to do it.

885
01:26:08,143 --> 01:26:10,228
I failed.

886
01:26:10,770 --> 01:26:13,523
I took too much time before I fought you.

887
01:26:15,150 --> 01:26:17,485
I'm going to run away now.

888
01:26:24,242 --> 01:26:25,827
Do you want to run away together?

889
01:26:27,287 --> 01:26:28,371
Huh?

890
01:26:29,164 --> 01:26:32,208
I can fight too.
You'll have a better chance at escaping.

891
01:26:34,252 --> 01:26:37,005
I killed lots of people.

892
01:26:37,088 --> 01:26:41,968
If you let me get away,
that would make you complicit in murder.

893
01:26:42,469 --> 01:26:44,012
Do you understand what that means?

894
01:26:45,221 --> 01:26:46,222
Uh...

895
01:26:46,806 --> 01:26:49,142
I know I shouldn't,
but I've got no choice.

896
01:26:49,643 --> 01:26:51,186
I still like you.

897
01:26:52,312 --> 01:26:54,147
You said it was all a lie.

898
01:26:54,230 --> 01:26:57,233
But you did teach me how to swim. Right?

899
01:27:39,442 --> 01:27:40,652
Hey!

900
01:27:40,735 --> 01:27:43,613
You should learn to be smarter.

901
01:27:43,697 --> 01:27:46,282
Reze! Hey, Reze!

902
01:27:51,955 --> 01:27:56,376
I'm going to be waiting
at the café at lunch!

903
01:27:56,459 --> 01:27:58,086
You'd better--

904
01:28:02,215 --> 01:28:05,135
Get up, Beam! My hand won't move!

905
01:28:06,302 --> 01:28:08,054
Rev up my engine!

906
01:28:52,599 --> 01:28:55,977
There's a fairy tale
that mothers in the Soviet Union tell

907
01:28:56,061 --> 01:28:57,062
when scolding their children.

908
01:28:58,188 --> 01:29:04,569
The story says that there's a secret room
in the military's munitions storehouse.

909
01:29:04,652 --> 01:29:06,571
And the secret room is filled
with orphans.

910
01:29:09,783 --> 01:29:12,285
The kids who live there
don't have any freedom.

911
01:29:12,368 --> 01:29:13,912
They're not allowed to go outside.

912
01:29:14,913 --> 01:29:16,456
They're treated like objects.

913
01:29:16,539 --> 01:29:19,459
And the military uses their bodies
for experiments until they die.

914
01:29:20,043 --> 01:29:22,587
It was supposed to be just a fairy tale.

915
01:29:23,088 --> 01:29:27,300
But one day, a newspaper reported that
that secret room really did exist.

916
01:29:28,176 --> 01:29:30,220
An American journalist was the one
who uncovered the story.

917
01:29:30,303 --> 01:29:32,180
It was all over the news.

918
01:29:32,680 --> 01:29:36,142
They published photos
of the children who were there.

919
01:29:36,643 --> 01:29:38,436
But the story soon disappeared.

920
01:29:39,020 --> 01:29:42,190
The girl who lured Denji in
was one of the kids from that room.

921
01:29:42,273 --> 01:29:43,316
TYPHOON DEVIL DAMAGE RELIEF FUND

922
01:29:43,399 --> 01:29:44,859
YOUR SUPPORT AND COOPERATION
ARE APPRECIATED

923
01:29:45,944 --> 01:29:49,614
A fighter created by the Soviet Union
to serve their country.

924
01:29:53,451 --> 01:29:56,955
They're called guinea pigs.

925
01:29:59,916 --> 01:30:04,337
The Yamabiko train bound for
Sendai will soon depart from Platform 12.

926
01:30:05,130 --> 01:30:07,132
The next stop will be Ueno.

927
01:30:07,215 --> 01:30:08,508
The train will now depart.

928
01:30:08,591 --> 01:30:10,760
This is the Yamabiko train
bound for Sendai.

929
01:30:10,844 --> 01:30:13,388
The train will now depart.
Doors are closing.

930
01:30:13,471 --> 01:30:15,473
Please stand clear of the closing doors.

931
01:31:28,171 --> 01:31:29,172
Me too.

932
01:31:31,883 --> 01:31:34,385
I like the country mouse too.

933
01:31:36,930 --> 01:31:40,308
One of my friends has a field
in the countryside.

934
01:31:41,184 --> 01:31:45,021
I go there to help out my friend
every year in the fall.

935
01:31:46,314 --> 01:31:51,027
The field has mice hiding in the soil
that damage the crops.

936
01:31:51,945 --> 01:31:56,074
We have to exterminate the mice
before the fields get covered in snow.

937
01:31:56,658 --> 01:32:02,121
So we dig up the fields and have the dogs
kill the mice hiding inside.

938
01:32:03,331 --> 01:32:04,540
I wonder why...

939
01:32:05,375 --> 01:32:06,960
whenever I watch...

940
01:32:08,378 --> 01:32:09,879
I feel so comforted.

941
01:32:15,343 --> 01:32:17,470
That's why I like the country mouse.

942
01:32:53,256 --> 01:32:54,340
Why...

943
01:32:55,383 --> 01:32:58,845
I wonder why I didn't kill you
the first time we met.

944
01:33:00,179 --> 01:33:03,224
Denji, to be honest...

945
01:33:04,976 --> 01:33:08,062
I've never been to school either.

946
01:33:21,200 --> 01:33:24,287
I told you to come with Hayakawa.

947
01:33:24,787 --> 01:33:28,374
You didn't want to make
Hayakawa kill a girl.

948
01:33:29,334 --> 01:33:30,543
You're so kind.

949
01:33:31,544 --> 01:33:33,921
It's because I'm an angel.

950
01:33:45,141 --> 01:33:46,142
Hey.

951
01:33:47,060 --> 01:33:48,728
Is the city a good place?

952
01:37:56,392 --> 01:37:59,437
Denji. I've got to close the café now.

953
01:38:01,022 --> 01:38:02,857
That girl was too cute.

954
01:38:03,524 --> 01:38:05,401
She was from a different world.

955
01:38:07,194 --> 01:38:10,990
I'm sure you'll meet a girl
who's perfect for you someday.

956
01:38:22,043 --> 01:38:23,711
RECOMMENDATIONS

957
01:38:37,558 --> 01:38:40,227
P-P-P-Power!

958
01:38:41,812 --> 01:38:47,151
I'm back! I tracked you down
by following your scent.

959
01:38:47,234 --> 01:38:49,737
What a tiny café!

960
01:38:56,994 --> 01:38:58,412
Hmm?

961
01:38:58,496 --> 01:39:01,123
Oh. What are you doing with those flowers?

962
01:39:01,207 --> 01:39:04,710
They would really suit me!
Give them to me!

963
01:39:19,225 --> 01:39:23,562
Hey! Don't eat them!
They're mine! You thief!

964
01:39:23,646 --> 01:39:25,606
You idiot!

965
01:39:25,690 --> 01:39:27,400
Spit them out right now!

966
01:39:27,900 --> 01:39:31,737
Spit them out! Spit them out!

